  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) for the Venezuela Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing political and socio-economic developments in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela (hereinafter Venezuela) have led to the outflow of millions of Venezuelans into neighbouring countries and beyond. The Latin America and Caribbean (LAC) region has never experienced, in modern history, such a large-scale movement of both migrants and refugees. Guided by the principle of &#x201c;leaving no one behind&#x201d; of the 2030 Agenda, this project implements an inclusive and comprehensive gender sensitive initiatives to help to eliminate barriers to equality and create better opportunities in order to make all population groups agents of change and improve their life. This project has been developed so that activities are included in the Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan 2022 and that respond to the above identified challenges faced by Venezuelan refugees and migrants, as well as host countries and communities. The project is being implemented with a principled and rights-based approach, upholding key standards of protection, accountability to affected populations, gender equality and data protection principles.</narrative>
  </description>
